WEBVTT

00:00:23.457 --> 00:00:27.418
&lt;i&gt;
Captain's log, stardate 58456.2.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:27.461 --> 00:00:30.682
&lt;i&gt;The&lt;/i&gt; Cerritos &lt;i&gt;is providing
support to the&lt;/i&gt; Vancouver.

00:00:30.725 --> 00:00:32.379
&lt;i&gt;Captain Nguyen will be reopening&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:32.423 --> 00:00:34.164
&lt;i&gt;postwar trade negotiations
with the Karemma,&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:34.207 --> 00:00:36.644
&lt;i&gt;a mercantile species
from the Gamma Quadrant,&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:36.688 --> 00:00:38.255
&lt;i&gt;while I will be overseeing
a delivery&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:38.298 --> 00:00:40.996
&lt;i&gt;of goodwill gifts
from the Alpha Quadrant,&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.521
&lt;i&gt;which will hopefully
sweeten the deal.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:43.564 --> 00:00:45.131
Captain, we have
an incoming communication

00:00:45.175 --> 00:00:46.306
from Starfleet Command.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:47.699
It's Admiral Buenamigo.

00:00:47.742 --> 00:00:49.962
- On-screen. &lt;i&gt;
- Captain Freeman.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:50.005 --> 00:00:52.182
Quite the payload
you've got us hauling.

00:00:52.225 --> 00:00:54.749
Are you trying to inebriate
half the Gamma Quadrant?

00:00:54.793 --> 00:00:56.577
&lt;i&gt;Anything to open up
communications.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:56.621 --> 00:00:59.276
&lt;i&gt;Speaking of which,
there's been a change of plans.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:59.319 --> 00:01:01.887
Don't tell me we need to pick up
more Andorian kegs.

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:03.802
&lt;i&gt; No.
The&lt;/i&gt; Cerritos &lt;i&gt;will be proceeding&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:03.845 --> 00:01:06.587
&lt;i&gt;to the rendezvous, but&lt;/i&gt; you &lt;i&gt;will
be negotiating with the Karemma.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:06.631 --> 00:01:09.329
I'm sorry, what?
But Captain Nguyen...

00:01:09.373 --> 00:01:11.853
&lt;i&gt;The&lt;/i&gt; Vancouver's &lt;i&gt;been rerouted
to the Hasparga system&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:11.897 --> 00:01:14.987
&lt;i&gt;to evacuate a colony being
threatened by a brown hole.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.989
W-Wait.
That-That's not even a thing...

00:01:17.032 --> 00:01:18.947
&lt;i&gt;Carol, this is our best chance
to heal scars&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:18.991 --> 00:01:20.340
&lt;i&gt;from the Dominion War.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:20.384 --> 00:01:21.820
&lt;i&gt;You have to make it work.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:21.863 --> 00:01:22.908
&lt;i&gt;Buenamigo out.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:22.951 --> 00:01:24.910
This is crazy.

00:01:24.953 --> 00:01:26.520
Anyone else would have months
to prepare

00:01:26.564 --> 00:01:28.131
- for this level of diplomacy.
- Captain Freeman,

00:01:28.174 --> 00:01:29.871
we're approaching
the rendezvous point.

00:01:30.916 --> 00:01:32.222
Bring us out of warp.

00:01:38.445 --> 00:01:40.012
Tacky Cardassian
fascist eyesore.

00:01:41.796 --> 00:01:44.886
Helm, just buy me some time
to read up on the Karemma.

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:47.367
- U-Uh, sir, h-how do we do that?

00:01:47.411 --> 00:01:49.456
Uh, I don't know.
Just circle around

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:51.502
and pretend
we're in awe of the pylons.

00:01:51.545 --> 00:01:52.894
Yes, sir.

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:13.132
- Um...
- Just keep circling.

00:03:29.382 --> 00:03:31.036
&lt;i&gt;
Aah! I can't believe&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:31.079 --> 00:03:32.820
we're at Deep Space Nine!

00:03:32.864 --> 00:03:34.909
I want to walk the Promenade.
Ooh, check out the stores.

00:03:34.953 --> 00:03:36.302
Oh, oh!
I bet they have a Quark's.

00:03:36.346 --> 00:03:38.086
Ho-ho, Tendi,
not just any Quark's--

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:39.566
the original Quark's!

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:41.046
You're excited
for a franchise restaurant?

00:03:41.089 --> 00:03:42.395
You guys are such tourists.

00:03:42.439 --> 00:03:44.049
We just got to move
a couple crates

00:03:44.092 --> 00:03:46.138
onto this Karemma ship,
and the rest of the day is ours!

00:03:46.181 --> 00:03:48.793
Y'all have fun with that. I'm
staying right here and relaxing.

00:03:48.836 --> 00:03:50.447
So does that mean
you're free today?

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:52.492
Oh, uh, hey. Thought-thought
you were still asleep.

00:03:52.536 --> 00:03:54.015
TENDI/RUTHERFORD/BOIMLER:
Hi, Jennifer!

00:03:54.059 --> 00:03:55.408
Hey, guys.

00:03:55.452 --> 00:03:57.062
So, I'm hanging
with my friends today,

00:03:57.105 --> 00:03:58.455
and I've been dying
for you to get to know them.

00:03:58.498 --> 00:04:01.240
Oh! Yeah, you know,
um, so I should--

00:04:01.284 --> 00:04:03.329
I'm gonna go give them a tour
of DS9,

00:04:03.373 --> 00:04:05.331
because... [chuckles] without
me, they'll probably get lost

00:04:05.375 --> 00:04:07.028
and end up in a mirror universe
with Smiley...

00:04:07.072 --> 00:04:08.421
- Oh, no, we won't.
- Yeah, we have maps!

00:04:08.465 --> 00:04:10.205
Mariner, you were just saying

00:04:10.249 --> 00:04:11.903
how you much you hate
this station.

00:04:11.946 --> 00:04:13.861
Why don't you stay here,
have some fun with Jennifer?

00:04:13.905 --> 00:04:15.907
Castro's hosting a salon today.

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:17.517
You're gonna love it. Mwah.

00:04:18.823 --> 00:04:21.173
Ooh, meeting the friends.
That's big.

00:04:21.216 --> 00:04:22.914
Oh, what if they're uptight
and judgy?

00:04:22.957 --> 00:04:24.524
I'm already not liking that they
call their hangouts "salons."

00:04:24.568 --> 00:04:26.439
Like, what are you, Hemingway?

00:04:26.483 --> 00:04:28.441
Well, Jennifer's going to care
if you can get along with them.

00:04:28.485 --> 00:04:30.574
- Oh, do you think?
- You'll be fine.

00:04:30.617 --> 00:04:32.010
Just don't be all bossy
like you are with us.

00:04:32.053 --> 00:04:34.534
- I'm not bossy!

00:04:34.578 --> 00:04:35.796
Okay, that was a good one, boss.

00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:45.240
- Oh, wow!
-Whoa!

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:46.807
The Promenade!

00:04:46.851 --> 00:04:48.809
Ooh, it's even more Cardassian
than I imagined.

00:04:48.853 --> 00:04:51.072
- Guys, this is awesome.
- Wow.

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:13.356
Captain Freeman,

00:05:13.399 --> 00:05:15.401
welcome to Deep Space Nine.

00:05:15.445 --> 00:05:16.707
Thank you, Colonel Kira.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.404
I trust you were informed

00:05:18.448 --> 00:05:20.319
that the &lt;i&gt;Vancouver&lt;/i&gt;
will no longer be joining us?

00:05:20.363 --> 00:05:22.060
Well, it's not Starfleet Command

00:05:22.103 --> 00:05:23.757
unless they throw us
a few curveballs.

00:05:23.801 --> 00:05:26.151
You got that right.

00:05:26.194 --> 00:05:29.154
Well, this is my first officer,
Commander Jack Ransom,

00:05:29.197 --> 00:05:30.590
and my security chief...

00:05:30.634 --> 00:05:32.766
Oh, I know
this scarred-up old barrowbug.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.203
- How are you, Shaxs?
- Any day not living

00:05:35.247 --> 00:05:37.031
under Cardassian rule
is a good one.

00:05:37.075 --> 00:05:39.033
We were in the Resistance together.

00:05:39.077 --> 00:05:41.775
He saved my life during a raid
on the Haru outposts.

00:05:41.819 --> 00:05:44.125
:
I still owe you for that one.

00:05:44.169 --> 00:05:45.997
:
No, you don't.

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:48.347
She saved &lt;i&gt;my&lt;/i&gt; life when
we were ambushed at Vannakur.

00:05:48.391 --> 00:05:50.480
Yeah, because I owed &lt;i&gt;you&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:50.523 --> 00:05:52.786
for pulling me out of that
plasma storm in the Badlands.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:55.441
I'm sure
it was all very rebellious.

00:05:55.485 --> 00:05:57.225
We wouldn't have even made it
to the Badlands

00:05:57.269 --> 00:05:59.227
if you hadn't sprung me
from that prison transport!

00:05:59.271 --> 00:06:00.751
You sprang me from one
the week before!

00:06:00.794 --> 00:06:01.795
That one didn't count!

00:06:01.839 --> 00:06:03.710
We were both locked up! Come on!

00:06:07.627 --> 00:06:11.152
Oh, these trade talks
are a waste of time.

00:06:11.196 --> 00:06:14.547
I don't know how these Alpha
savages managed to win the war.

00:06:14.591 --> 00:06:17.158
Neither do I.
But if there's even a chance

00:06:17.202 --> 00:06:18.551
at making a profit,

00:06:18.595 --> 00:06:19.596
I'll hear them out.

00:06:19.639 --> 00:06:21.598
And if diplomacy fails,

00:06:21.641 --> 00:06:24.427
we always have the other option.

00:06:32.783 --> 00:06:34.175
Uh, hey, can you sign my PADD?

00:06:34.219 --> 00:06:35.176
Of course!

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:37.178
I love my fans.

00:06:37.222 --> 00:06:39.920
For a small price, plus bar tax
and processing fees.

00:06:41.313 --> 00:06:43.533
Quark. Sorry to interrupt.

00:06:43.576 --> 00:06:45.622
This is Captain Freeman
of the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:45.665 --> 00:06:48.363
She and her crew are here
on important Starfleet duty.

00:06:48.407 --> 00:06:50.801
Ah, you look radiant, Captain!

00:06:50.844 --> 00:06:52.063
Uh... pass.

00:06:52.106 --> 00:06:54.195
I love Starfleet.

00:06:54.239 --> 00:06:57.242
I do a lot of business
in Federation space.

00:06:57.285 --> 00:06:59.418
Quark is
our resident entrepreneur.

00:06:59.462 --> 00:07:02.508
I did expand my simple bar
into 21 franchises

00:07:02.552 --> 00:07:04.292
across the Alpha Quadrant.

00:07:04.336 --> 00:07:05.511
And somehow

00:07:05.555 --> 00:07:07.252
- I remain humble.
- What are

00:07:07.295 --> 00:07:09.167
you talking about? Can't people
just replicate drinks?

00:07:09.210 --> 00:07:11.822
None of your outdated
Starfleet replicators

00:07:11.865 --> 00:07:13.650
can make what I have to offer.

00:07:13.693 --> 00:07:17.088
My unique design gives our
refreshments that special zing.

00:07:17.131 --> 00:07:19.351
I've been crafting them
for years.

00:07:19.394 --> 00:07:21.701
So, Captain,
do you think there's room

00:07:21.745 --> 00:07:23.790
at Starfleet Academy
for a Quark's?

00:07:23.834 --> 00:07:25.531
Um... no.

00:07:25.575 --> 00:07:28.186
Not to worry. We'll set you up
with a Quark's Express.

00:07:28.229 --> 00:07:29.970
I gave one to the Bolians.
They love it.

00:07:30.014 --> 00:07:31.494
- Whoa!

00:07:31.537 --> 00:07:32.799
- The original Quark's! Oh, man.
- Ooh, ooh,

00:07:32.843 --> 00:07:34.105
let's get some seats at the bar.

00:07:34.148 --> 00:07:36.281
Oh, my stars. They've got dabo.

00:07:36.324 --> 00:07:38.457
- I-I thought it was illegal.
- Dabo!

00:07:38.501 --> 00:07:39.763
Boimler, it's probably rigged.

00:07:39.806 --> 00:07:41.591
Ho-ho-ho, cheating?
At a Quark's?

00:07:41.634 --> 00:07:43.114
You can't rig a game here.

00:07:43.157 --> 00:07:44.419
Besides, I'm Bold Boimler,

00:07:44.463 --> 00:07:46.291
and fortune favors the bold!

00:07:46.334 --> 00:07:47.422
Oh! Oh, God.

00:07:47.466 --> 00:07:48.511
- Oh, sorry. Sorry.
- Uh...

00:07:48.554 --> 00:07:50.643
Ho-ho-ho! A fellow Orion!

00:07:50.687 --> 00:07:52.602
- Greetings.
- Hey, look at that!

00:07:52.645 --> 00:07:54.342
- That's awesome!
- Oh, wow, hi.

00:07:54.386 --> 00:07:56.040
I'm Tendi.
This is my friend Rutherford.

00:07:56.083 --> 00:07:57.955
I'm Mesk. I got to tell you,

00:07:57.998 --> 00:08:00.044
I never run into
other Orions in Starfleet.

00:08:00.087 --> 00:08:02.089
Me neither. I guess
there's just not a lot of us.

00:08:02.133 --> 00:08:03.743
Tendi. T-Tendi.

00:08:03.787 --> 00:08:05.528
Is your family
from the Northern Hemisphere?

00:08:05.571 --> 00:08:07.007
Evtan Rim, right?

00:08:07.051 --> 00:08:08.574
Uh, they-they
kind of moved around a lot.

00:08:08.618 --> 00:08:10.924
So...
Deep Space Nine--

00:08:10.968 --> 00:08:14.537
it's got to be so cool serving
right next to the wormhole, huh?

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:17.017
Oh, yeah. We get
some pretty shady characters

00:08:17.061 --> 00:08:18.149
coming through here.

00:08:18.192 --> 00:08:19.716
Our kind of people, am I right?

00:08:19.759 --> 00:08:20.891
- Oh, yeah. No, totally.

00:08:20.934 --> 00:08:22.545
- Shady.
- Yeah.

00:08:22.588 --> 00:08:24.024
Uh, Rutherford, do you want

00:08:24.068 --> 00:08:24.851
to get food with our drinks
so that we...

00:08:24.895 --> 00:08:26.374
Oh, cool. Awesome.

00:08:26.418 --> 00:08:28.159
Hey, check this out--
my Orion multi-key.

00:08:28.202 --> 00:08:31.597
I got a religious exemption
to wear it with my uniform.

00:08:31.641 --> 00:08:32.598
Suckers.

00:08:32.642 --> 00:08:34.469
Whoa! What is it?

00:08:34.513 --> 00:08:38.430
Uh, it's a traditional tool
used by Orion pirates.

00:08:38.473 --> 00:08:39.605
Aw, it's good for everything--

00:08:39.649 --> 00:08:41.128
from stabbing guys

00:08:41.172 --> 00:08:43.522
to picking locks
to stealing ships...

00:08:43.566 --> 00:08:45.698
Oh, wow! Yeah,
all positive things.

00:08:45.742 --> 00:08:47.439
Say, I just got off duty.

00:08:47.482 --> 00:08:49.310
You guys want the grand tour?

00:08:49.354 --> 00:08:51.008
- Oh, I think we're...
- Definitely!

00:08:51.051 --> 00:08:52.966
Let's go around this circle!

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:54.577
All right! Come with me!

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:56.753
This is great.
Couple of Orions up to no good,

00:08:56.796 --> 00:08:58.842
just skulking around.

00:08:58.885 --> 00:09:00.844
Lock up your valuables,
am I right?

00:09:00.887 --> 00:09:02.019
- Ha. Yeah.

00:09:02.062 --> 00:09:03.716
Totally.

00:09:05.022 --> 00:09:06.850
All right. Here we go.

00:09:07.894 --> 00:09:09.374
- Ooh! Look who's here!
- Mariner!

00:09:09.417 --> 00:09:10.810
Hey, girl!

00:09:10.854 --> 00:09:12.507
Hey! What's... up?

00:09:12.551 --> 00:09:15.293
Finally we get to meet
the mysterious Lady Mariner.

00:09:15.336 --> 00:09:17.861
I don't even mind
you're so late.

00:09:17.904 --> 00:09:20.037
Wow, looking profesh
in the uniform.

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:21.908
I-I didn't get the memo
that, uh,

00:09:21.952 --> 00:09:23.649
this was like
a sweats kind of party.

00:09:23.693 --> 00:09:25.346
Not a party-- a salon.

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:27.740
And we always set the wardrobe
as Betazoid casual.

00:09:27.784 --> 00:09:29.437
Jenny didn't tell you?

00:09:29.481 --> 00:09:30.656
They call you Jenny?

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:31.918
Ugh, I hate it.

00:09:31.962 --> 00:09:33.398
It goes back to our time
at the Academy.

00:09:33.441 --> 00:09:35.400
Okay, everyone, grab a wick.

00:09:35.443 --> 00:09:37.924
These candles
aren't going to dip themselves.

00:09:37.968 --> 00:09:39.186
Candle-making.

00:09:39.230 --> 00:09:41.014
&lt;i&gt;Very&lt;/i&gt; cool.

00:09:41.058 --> 00:09:42.668
And this is obvious,
but don't forget

00:09:42.712 --> 00:09:44.148
to set an intention
when you light it

00:09:44.191 --> 00:09:45.410
or you're just gonna be wasting
the wax.

00:09:45.453 --> 00:09:46.977
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:48.282
Um, I'm just gonna make
a quick, uh, pit stop

00:09:48.326 --> 00:09:50.197
before I dive into the dipping.

00:09:52.156 --> 00:09:53.940
Hey, girl, can we talk Boimler?

00:09:53.984 --> 00:09:55.463
Oh, I know what
you're gonna ask,

00:09:55.507 --> 00:09:56.813
and, no, he's
actually not reverse-aging.

00:09:56.856 --> 00:09:58.031
He just doesn't get
enough vitamins.

00:09:58.075 --> 00:09:59.467
- Is he single?
- What?

00:09:59.511 --> 00:10:00.773
Purple hair is so sexy.

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:05.778
Yeah, I'm gonna just need
a &lt;i&gt;little&lt;/i&gt; more of this.

00:10:05.822 --> 00:10:07.432
Oh. Oh. Ooh.

00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:13.830
Trade Minister Korzak,
this is Captain Freeman of...

00:10:13.873 --> 00:10:16.223
I was told I would be meeting
with Captain Nguyen!

00:10:16.267 --> 00:10:18.182
How are we supposed
to negotiate a trade agreement

00:10:18.225 --> 00:10:19.792
when you can't even honor
an appointment?!

00:10:19.836 --> 00:10:20.924
- I won't have it!

00:10:20.967 --> 00:10:23.056
Understandable but unfortunate,

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:26.059
because we did bring
some rather fine gifts.

00:10:26.103 --> 00:10:27.060
I don't...

00:10:27.104 --> 00:10:28.583
Gifts, you say?

00:10:28.627 --> 00:10:30.803
Well, we're already here.

00:10:30.847 --> 00:10:32.587
We may as well proceed.

00:10:32.631 --> 00:10:33.980
Excellent.

00:10:34.024 --> 00:10:35.416
The commerce opportunities
are endless

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:36.809
on this side of the wormhole.

00:10:36.853 --> 00:10:37.941
- I think you'll find...
- I owe &lt;i&gt;you&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:37.984 --> 00:10:39.159
for taking a phaser shot for me

00:10:39.203 --> 00:10:40.421
- on the Da'Karo mission.
- What?

00:10:40.465 --> 00:10:41.814
You took one for &lt;i&gt;me&lt;/i&gt; at Da'Karo.

00:10:41.858 --> 00:10:43.381
No, I mean Da'Karo Prime--

00:10:43.424 --> 00:10:44.687
the one with the little trees!

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:46.427
I don't remember that. No way.

00:10:46.471 --> 00:10:48.081
Nerys!

00:10:49.561 --> 00:10:51.258
Whoa, that's
Chief O'Brien's dartboard!

00:10:51.302 --> 00:10:53.260
Look at that!
Bajoran food court!

00:10:53.304 --> 00:10:55.480
Ho-ho!
Oh, I should tone it down.

00:10:55.523 --> 00:10:57.351
Hey, so,
does your family approve

00:10:57.395 --> 00:10:58.831
of you being in Starfleet?

00:10:58.875 --> 00:11:00.441
You know, they had
some thoughts, but, uh,

00:11:00.485 --> 00:11:02.400
- for the most part...
- Pfft! Orion values.

00:11:02.443 --> 00:11:04.750
My folks definitely wanted me to
take over the family business,

00:11:04.794 --> 00:11:06.621
and I was like,
"No, thanks, Mom!"

00:11:06.665 --> 00:11:08.536
Wait, you mean, like,
the pirate business?

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:09.712
Hey, you said it, not me.

00:11:09.755 --> 00:11:10.713
- Ooh-hoo-hoo!

00:11:10.756 --> 00:11:12.236
Wait right here!

00:11:12.279 --> 00:11:13.237
I got to dangle
my legs off the second story

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:14.891
like in the holovids!

00:11:14.934 --> 00:11:16.414
- So, real talk--

00:11:16.457 --> 00:11:17.981
what's the first ship
you ever stole, ma?

00:11:18.024 --> 00:11:20.331
Um, actually,
I don't do that stuff.

00:11:20.374 --> 00:11:22.202
Oh, yeah. No, no, no.
Me neither.

00:11:22.246 --> 00:11:25.205
Look, not every Orion does
the pirate criminal thing, okay?

00:11:25.249 --> 00:11:28.208
Whoa! Easy! I'm starting to feel

00:11:28.252 --> 00:11:31.081
some of those aggressive
female pheromones firing off.

00:11:31.124 --> 00:11:32.604
- We don't all have those!
- Tendi!

00:11:32.647 --> 00:11:34.171
Look at me! Tendi!

00:11:34.214 --> 00:11:35.215
&lt;i&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
Cerritos &lt;i&gt;crew, I need a detail&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:35.259 --> 00:11:36.913
&lt;i&gt;to transfer gift pallets over to&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:36.956 --> 00:11:38.001
&lt;i&gt;- the Karemma ship.&lt;/i&gt;
- Are you looking? Look at me!

00:11:38.044 --> 00:11:39.785
I'll do it, Captain. Oh, gosh.

00:11:39.829 --> 00:11:41.221
- Captain needs us on duty ASAP.
- Tendi! Tendi! Tendi!

00:11:41.265 --> 00:11:42.832
Oh, what a shame.
Rutherford, let's go!

00:11:42.875 --> 00:11:44.181
But I wanted to have
a heart-to-heart

00:11:44.224 --> 00:11:45.791
with a junior reporter up here!

00:11:45.835 --> 00:11:47.793
- Now!
- Aw, man.

00:11:49.316 --> 00:11:50.753
Dabo!

00:11:50.796 --> 00:11:53.103
And the streak continues.

00:11:53.146 --> 00:11:56.367
It looks like we've got a bit
of beginner's luck on our hands.

00:11:56.410 --> 00:11:58.935
Surprising for a man
with a coin purse.

00:11:58.978 --> 00:12:01.502
It's a clutch.
And it's feeling a little light.

00:12:01.546 --> 00:12:02.982
- Let it ride!

00:12:07.117 --> 00:12:09.075
Man, it must have been so cool

00:12:09.119 --> 00:12:10.990
for you to hang out
with another Orion.

00:12:11.034 --> 00:12:13.732
Yeah, sure. But, actually, I'd
rather just be working with you.

00:12:13.776 --> 00:12:15.473
-  Oh!
- Hey-oh!

00:12:15.516 --> 00:12:17.475
Guess who got themselves
reassigned! I'm doing security

00:12:17.518 --> 00:12:19.607
for you guys
for the rest of the day.

00:12:19.651 --> 00:12:20.957
How lucky are you?

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:22.741
Mesk!
That's great!

00:12:22.785 --> 00:12:25.135
Oh, wow. That's... that's news.

00:12:25.178 --> 00:12:27.615
Hey! This calls for
a little pirate shanty!

00:12:27.659 --> 00:12:29.792
Tendi, sing along!
I know you know it!

00:12:29.835 --> 00:12:32.620
&lt;i&gt;♪ Where it's cold and dark
in the void of space♪&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:32.664 --> 00:12:35.362
&lt;i&gt;♪ Orions take from every race!♪&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:40.367 --> 00:12:41.847
&lt;i&gt;
It was a dark and stormy&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:41.891 --> 00:12:43.806
57162.3.

00:12:43.849 --> 00:12:45.633
A stardate just like this.

00:12:45.677 --> 00:12:47.984
Castro really nailed
the theme tonight, didn't she?

00:12:48.027 --> 00:12:49.855
And what is the theme?
Uh, pillows?

00:12:49.899 --> 00:12:51.161
"Personal Battlefields."

00:12:51.204 --> 00:12:52.771
Oh, great,
'cause this one is mine.

00:12:52.815 --> 00:12:55.165
...that really I wasn't
in the &lt;i&gt;Enterprise,&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:55.208 --> 00:12:58.037
the &lt;i&gt;Enterprise&lt;/i&gt;
was in me all along.

00:12:58.081 --> 00:12:59.560
Oh, my gosh,
you guys, thank you.

00:12:59.604 --> 00:13:01.084
- Ugh, yes. Speak the truth.
- Yeah.

00:13:01.127 --> 00:13:02.172
- Speak it, honey. Speak.
- So good.

00:13:02.215 --> 00:13:03.869
And now, please welcome

00:13:03.913 --> 00:13:05.828
a new voice, Mariner.

00:13:07.264 --> 00:13:10.441
Me? Oh, no, uh, I mean,
I didn't prepare anything.

00:13:10.484 --> 00:13:12.573
That's okay,
just speak your truth.

00:13:12.617 --> 00:13:14.837
Yeah, I'd rather just listen
to y'all's truths.

00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:16.490
Okay, I'm just gonna say it.

00:13:16.534 --> 00:13:18.318
The intention I'm detecting
is that you're kind of

00:13:18.362 --> 00:13:20.059
disrespecting my salon.

00:13:20.103 --> 00:13:21.974
Oh, no, I don't want to
disrespect anything, um, I...

00:13:22.018 --> 00:13:24.542
Jenny was right,
you do love being contrary.

00:13:24.585 --> 00:13:26.631
- Anya, you want to go next?
- Oh, yeah.

00:13:26.674 --> 00:13:29.852
Of course. I call this piece
"The Kobayashi Maroon."

00:13:29.895 --> 00:13:32.245
There's no right way
to dance it.

00:13:38.861 --> 00:13:40.514
As you can see,

00:13:40.558 --> 00:13:42.777
species from all over
the quadrant are participating

00:13:42.821 --> 00:13:45.345
in a robust exchange
of goods and services

00:13:45.389 --> 00:13:46.912
right here on Deep Space Nine.

00:13:46.956 --> 00:13:49.915
A tailor and some
tchotchke kiosks?

00:13:49.959 --> 00:13:51.917
This is hardly worth my time.

00:13:51.961 --> 00:13:53.919
Well, what about Quark's?
He started

00:13:53.963 --> 00:13:56.922
his bar here and now has
locations on dozens of planets.

00:13:56.966 --> 00:13:58.924
Franchises, you say?

00:13:58.968 --> 00:14:01.405
Yes, and with massive profits.

00:14:01.448 --> 00:14:04.451
Nobody can tell you better
than the Ferengi himself.

00:14:06.932 --> 00:14:10.022
I was so impressed with
your entrepreneurial story.

00:14:10.066 --> 00:14:12.503
I believe our friends
from the Gamma Quadrant

00:14:12.546 --> 00:14:13.939
would love to hear all about it.

00:14:13.983 --> 00:14:15.723
Uh, I'm too busy.

00:14:15.767 --> 00:14:17.943
Quark, you've had such success,

00:14:17.987 --> 00:14:19.640
Korzak could open up even more

00:14:19.684 --> 00:14:21.642
- franchise locations in his...
- Pass.

00:14:21.686 --> 00:14:23.340
I don't want
to oversaturate the market.

00:14:23.383 --> 00:14:25.124
Do us a favor here, Quark,

00:14:25.168 --> 00:14:26.691
we're trying to make
a good impression.

00:14:26.734 --> 00:14:29.259
Maybe I don't want
to make a good impression.

00:14:29.302 --> 00:14:31.130
Oh? And why is that?

00:14:31.174 --> 00:14:33.393
A little thing called
the Dominion War?

00:14:33.437 --> 00:14:35.308
I don't remember
the Karemma helping out

00:14:35.352 --> 00:14:37.310
when my customers were dying!

00:14:37.354 --> 00:14:38.790
We had nothing
to do with that.

00:14:38.833 --> 00:14:39.922
The Founders and the Vorta
were behind...

00:14:39.965 --> 00:14:42.837
Oh, right, you were so innocent.

00:14:42.881 --> 00:14:45.014
I've done business
with your kind before.

00:14:45.057 --> 00:14:47.538
I'm not dumb enough
to repeat that mistake.

00:14:47.581 --> 00:14:49.453
You bring me here to be insulted

00:14:49.496 --> 00:14:51.368
by this long-lobed halfling?

00:14:51.411 --> 00:14:53.196
- Hey! No. No!
- Ugh, the nerve.

00:14:53.239 --> 00:14:55.633
&lt;i&gt;
♪ And 40 slaves♪&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:55.676 --> 00:14:57.330
&lt;i&gt;♪ To serve our days♪&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:57.374 --> 00:15:00.203
&lt;i&gt;♪ And we'll kill you
in your cots.♪&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:00.246 --> 00:15:02.205
Feels weird being "let in"

00:15:02.248 --> 00:15:03.946
instead of breaking in,
you know?

00:15:03.989 --> 00:15:06.209
If I don't pick a lock,
I get all jittery. I'm all,

00:15:06.252 --> 00:15:08.037
"How did I get in here?"
I know you feel me.

00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:09.864
Seriously, Tends,
I bet the two of us

00:15:09.908 --> 00:15:12.258
could take this ship if we
wanted to. [laughs] You know?

00:15:12.302 --> 00:15:14.043
Would you just shut up?!

00:15:14.086 --> 00:15:16.784
You keep acting like pirating
is cool, but guess what.

00:15:16.828 --> 00:15:18.525
It's not. It's embarrassing,

00:15:18.569 --> 00:15:21.267
a-and sometimes it makes me
not want to be associated

00:15:21.311 --> 00:15:23.661
- with Orions at all.
- Wow.

00:15:23.704 --> 00:15:26.011
Someone got all "human'ed up"
at the Academy.

00:15:26.055 --> 00:15:28.883
At least I'll remember
where we came from.

00:15:28.927 --> 00:15:30.276
- Dabo!

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:32.104
Oh, he does it again!

00:15:32.148 --> 00:15:33.714
Hey, man, get off me.
What are you doing?

00:15:33.758 --> 00:15:35.281
You're cheating, human.

00:15:35.325 --> 00:15:37.762
- Tell me your secret.
- I'm not cheating.

00:15:37.805 --> 00:15:40.721
I'm just the Dabo king.
In fact, triple

00:15:40.765 --> 00:15:42.462
- down Dabo.

00:15:44.638 --> 00:15:46.162
What is wrong with you?

00:15:46.205 --> 00:15:48.642
- I have principles.
- No, you don't.

00:15:48.686 --> 00:15:51.036
Quark, Korzak,
please calm down.

00:15:51.080 --> 00:15:53.778
I will not stand
for this disrespect.

00:15:53.821 --> 00:15:56.955
I know, I know. Sometimes Quark
can come across a little...

00:15:56.999 --> 00:15:58.435
- insufferable.

00:15:58.478 --> 00:16:01.481
But his business acumen?
Oh, it speaks for itself.

00:16:01.525 --> 00:16:04.789
He's got this amazing
replicator, the Quark 2000.

00:16:04.832 --> 00:16:06.399
You know,
I've never seen anything

00:16:06.443 --> 00:16:09.011
- like it.
- This is the Quark 2000?

00:16:09.054 --> 00:16:11.970
Hey, get away from that!
That's my intellectual property.

00:16:12.014 --> 00:16:13.624
Quark, be reasonable.

00:16:13.667 --> 00:16:16.061
That's it. Everyone,
out of the bar. We're closed.

00:16:16.105 --> 00:16:18.063
Are you kidding? Minister.

00:16:18.107 --> 00:16:20.196
That replicator contains
trade secrets.

00:16:20.239 --> 00:16:22.807
Kira, they're
trying to rip me off.

00:16:22.850 --> 00:16:25.070
- How dare you?

00:16:25.114 --> 00:16:26.593
Korzak.

00:16:26.637 --> 00:16:28.856
- Alpha contingency, now.

00:16:38.605 --> 00:16:40.259
Ow, hot wax!

00:16:40.303 --> 00:16:43.132
- Get off of me. Help!

00:16:44.263 --> 00:16:46.091
Kira to ops.

00:16:46.135 --> 00:16:48.441
That thing must have triggered
some kind of system shutdown.

00:16:48.485 --> 00:16:49.747
You might have sold them
on his franchise

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:51.270
a little too well, Captain.

00:16:51.314 --> 00:16:53.533
Ugh, how did we get
from failed trade talks

00:16:53.577 --> 00:16:55.187
to a kidnapping?

00:16:57.276 --> 00:16:59.670
- Dabo!
- No!

00:17:03.195 --> 00:17:05.458
- Hey, Mesk, what are you doing?
- Oh, this? It's nothing.

00:17:05.502 --> 00:17:07.808
Just a little pirate code
for future Orions

00:17:07.852 --> 00:17:09.767
to let them know
D'Vana Tendi is a traitor!

00:17:09.810 --> 00:17:12.683
I'm not a traitor. I just,
I don't feel the need to...

00:17:12.726 --> 00:17:14.032
Help! Help!

00:17:16.165 --> 00:17:17.601
Is that-is that Quark?

00:17:17.644 --> 00:17:20.256
This is all
a misunderstanding.

00:17:20.299 --> 00:17:21.779
Oh, you say?

00:17:21.822 --> 00:17:24.129
Release docking and set a course
for the wormhole.

00:17:35.967 --> 00:17:37.664
I can't get the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:37.708 --> 00:17:39.449
We're trapped!

00:17:41.146 --> 00:17:43.888
Um, why did we just lose power?

00:17:43.931 --> 00:17:45.846
I bet it has something to do
with the wormhole.

00:17:45.890 --> 00:17:47.370
Ooh, yeah. It's always something
with the wormhole.

00:17:47.413 --> 00:17:48.371
Let's get to our stations.

00:17:50.503 --> 00:17:52.114
The manual latch is fused.

00:17:52.157 --> 00:17:53.680
Excuse me,
is anybody-- is anyone else

00:17:53.724 --> 00:17:55.334
- finding it hard to breathe?
- Come on,

00:17:55.378 --> 00:17:56.683
we've been in here two seconds.
It's totally fine.

00:17:56.727 --> 00:17:58.163
It's...

00:17:58.207 --> 00:18:00.034
- Wait, it is a little stuffy.
- I need air!

00:18:00.078 --> 00:18:01.601
Everybody, just keep calm, okay?

00:18:01.645 --> 00:18:02.820
- What is going on?
- Oh, my God!

00:18:02.863 --> 00:18:05.344
Ah, the Impulian candles.

00:18:05.388 --> 00:18:06.780
The flames eat twice the oxygen.

00:18:06.824 --> 00:18:08.042
- Wait, wait, wait,

00:18:08.086 --> 00:18:09.131
our intentions.

00:18:09.174 --> 00:18:10.175
Everybody, okay,

00:18:10.219 --> 00:18:11.220
let's calm down, all right?

00:18:13.178 --> 00:18:14.701
If I could have
your attention, please.

00:18:14.745 --> 00:18:16.486
Ladies.

00:18:16.529 --> 00:18:19.097
Why are you being so polite?
This doesn't sound like you.

00:18:19.141 --> 00:18:20.751
Because I've been trying
this whole time

00:18:20.794 --> 00:18:23.014
not to be bossy or mean
to your friends.

00:18:23.057 --> 00:18:25.190
- Why?
- Because if they didn't like me,

00:18:25.234 --> 00:18:27.192
you'd get mad
and this wouldn't work out.

00:18:27.236 --> 00:18:30.630
Beckett, I like that you
don't take [bleep] from anyone.

00:18:30.674 --> 00:18:32.502
- Really?
- Yes.

00:18:32.545 --> 00:18:34.199
I know my friends
can be a bit much.

00:18:34.243 --> 00:18:36.854
I've been looking forward to you
tearing them a new one.

00:18:36.897 --> 00:18:38.682
Go destroy them.

00:18:38.725 --> 00:18:40.249
Thanks, babe.

00:18:40.292 --> 00:18:42.207
- Everyone, shut the [bleep] up!

00:18:42.251 --> 00:18:45.297
Ugh. You can't tell us
what to do. This is my salon.

00:18:45.341 --> 00:18:46.777
- And this is my phaser.

00:18:46.820 --> 00:18:48.387
Hey, did you know that,
when you're unconscious,

00:18:48.431 --> 00:18:50.128
you actually consume
way less oxygen?

00:18:50.172 --> 00:18:51.956
So? What does that
have to do...

00:18:51.999 --> 00:18:54.393
- Oh, my God, she stunned her.
-  What are you doing?

00:18:54.437 --> 00:18:57.135
- Just actualizing my dreams.
- No!

00:19:07.537 --> 00:19:10.104
Oh, man, we're almost
to the wormhole!

00:19:10.148 --> 00:19:11.193
Mesk.

00:19:11.236 --> 00:19:12.933
Mesk, you can save us!

00:19:12.977 --> 00:19:15.240
- Um, I'm sorry, what?
- With all your pirating skills.

00:19:15.284 --> 00:19:17.242
You can take the ship
Orion-style.

00:19:17.286 --> 00:19:20.680
Right, totally.
Um, the, uh, thing with that is,

00:19:20.724 --> 00:19:21.899
um... I, uh...

00:19:21.942 --> 00:19:23.857
I don't know how.
I've never

00:19:23.901 --> 00:19:25.729
pirated anything
in my whole stupid life.

00:19:25.772 --> 00:19:28.732
- What? It's all you talk about!
- I'm a faker.

00:19:28.775 --> 00:19:32.388
I don't know. I've, I've
never even been to Orion.

00:19:32.431 --> 00:19:33.954
I-I'm from Cincinnati.

00:19:33.998 --> 00:19:36.305
- What? Cincinnati?
- Are you freaking serious?

00:19:36.348 --> 00:19:38.307
I got adopted by humans,

00:19:38.350 --> 00:19:40.004
and everything
I know about Orions

00:19:40.047 --> 00:19:41.701
I learned from the holonovels.

00:19:41.745 --> 00:19:44.269
Bad ones, too. The ones
with the boobs on the cover.

00:19:44.313 --> 00:19:45.749
Why would you lie?

00:19:45.792 --> 00:19:47.490
Well, people just expect Orions

00:19:47.533 --> 00:19:49.579
to act like that,
so it's always worked for me.

00:19:49.622 --> 00:19:51.189
I never knew any other Orions

00:19:51.233 --> 00:19:53.670
back in Ohio, so no one
ever checked me on it.

00:19:55.367 --> 00:19:57.151
Yeah, I-I get that.

00:19:57.195 --> 00:19:59.371
It's hard when you feel like
people expect you to act

00:19:59.415 --> 00:20:01.982
a certain way, but you just
got to be yourself.

00:20:02.026 --> 00:20:03.767
It doesn't matter
what other people expect.

00:20:03.810 --> 00:20:06.204
I'm sorry that I put
all that on you, too.

00:20:06.248 --> 00:20:09.251
Thanks, and I'm sure
the real Mesk is great, too.

00:20:09.294 --> 00:20:10.687
The Ohio Mesk.

00:20:10.730 --> 00:20:13.777
Ugh, I just feel bad
'cause actual

00:20:13.820 --> 00:20:16.475
Orion pirating skills really
would come in handy right now.

00:20:16.519 --> 00:20:19.043
Yup, you're right about that.

00:20:19.086 --> 00:20:21.045
- Whoa.

00:20:21.088 --> 00:20:22.612
What the...?

00:20:24.178 --> 00:20:26.746
Listen, if there's one thing
my father taught me,

00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:29.009
it's that every ship
has a security fail-safe.

00:20:29.053 --> 00:20:31.447
Your family's Orion pirates?

00:20:31.490 --> 00:20:33.536
Yup, Syndicate and all.

00:20:35.538 --> 00:20:37.801
- You there, stop.

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:51.728
- Wait a minute, wait a minute.

00:20:51.771 --> 00:20:52.772
That thing has a tooth remover?

00:20:52.816 --> 00:20:55.166
Shh, I'm pirating. Let's go!

00:20:57.864 --> 00:20:59.997
Whoa, you just did that
with a wine opener!

00:21:04.958 --> 00:21:06.525
Oh, no!

00:21:06.569 --> 00:21:07.918
Wormhole!

00:21:22.367 --> 00:21:23.716
You stopped us? How?

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:25.283
I used the latinum
from the guy's tooth

00:21:25.327 --> 00:21:27.241
to magnetically decouple
the propulsion controls.

00:21:27.285 --> 00:21:29.418
You took the ship...
You took the ship!

00:21:29.461 --> 00:21:31.376
Ugh, my folks would be so proud,

00:21:31.420 --> 00:21:32.986
but this is only
a temporary fix.

00:21:33.030 --> 00:21:34.510
In a couple of hours,

00:21:34.553 --> 00:21:35.946
the Karemma are gonna
figure out what I did,

00:21:35.989 --> 00:21:36.816
- and when they do... Whoa!

00:21:36.860 --> 00:21:38.775
We're in a tractor beam.

00:21:38.818 --> 00:21:40.864
&lt;i&gt; We're saved.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:40.907 --> 00:21:42.169
We got 'em.

00:21:42.213 --> 00:21:43.432
Good work, people.

00:21:43.475 --> 00:21:45.129
Wonder why they
just stopped and waited.

00:21:45.172 --> 00:21:46.783
I mean, they were
as good as Gamma'd.

00:21:46.826 --> 00:21:49.916
Beam 'em to the brig first,
ask questions later.

00:21:49.960 --> 00:21:52.354
Well, I definitely didn't have

00:21:52.397 --> 00:21:54.573
"phaser all your friends"
on my bingo card.

00:21:54.617 --> 00:21:56.270
And that's what I like
about us--

00:21:56.314 --> 00:21:58.360
you keep things unexpected.

00:21:58.403 --> 00:22:02.015
Though, you know, us being
the only ones not stunned here?

00:22:02.059 --> 00:22:03.408
Kind of a bad look.

00:22:03.452 --> 00:22:04.757
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm, mm-hmm.
I see that.

00:22:04.801 --> 00:22:07.325
Welp, shall we?

00:22:07.369 --> 00:22:08.631
Mwah.

00:22:17.466 --> 00:22:20.599
Let me out of here. This
imprisonment will not stand.

00:22:20.643 --> 00:22:22.645
You kidnapped
an innocent Ferengi.

00:22:22.688 --> 00:22:24.037
If I can quickly interject,

00:22:24.081 --> 00:22:26.126
this is just
a big misunderstanding,

00:22:26.170 --> 00:22:29.129
and I'm sure we can work out
some sort of resolution.

00:22:29.173 --> 00:22:32.437
A resolution for what?
You stole our technology.

00:22:32.481 --> 00:22:35.701
- Your technology?
- The Quark 2000.

00:22:35.745 --> 00:22:37.311
He stole it from us.

00:22:37.355 --> 00:22:39.488
It's filled
with Karemma components.

00:22:39.531 --> 00:22:40.750
So, you didn't kidnap him?

00:22:40.793 --> 00:22:42.926
No. We arrested him.

00:22:44.101 --> 00:22:46.799
I may have borrowed

00:22:46.843 --> 00:22:48.627
a Karemma replicator
some years ago,

00:22:48.671 --> 00:22:51.848
but it was my codes
that made it so popular.

00:22:51.891 --> 00:22:53.632
Oh, that's beside the point.

00:22:53.676 --> 00:22:56.809
I think I have a solution
that will make you both happy.

00:22:58.942 --> 00:23:00.770
&lt;i&gt;
Captain's log, supplemental.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:00.813 --> 00:23:02.641
&lt;i&gt;Our mission, though unexpected,&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:02.685 --> 00:23:04.817
&lt;i&gt;has been a resounding success.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:04.861 --> 00:23:07.341
&lt;i&gt;The Karemma have agreed
to open up trade&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:07.385 --> 00:23:08.604
&lt;i&gt;and not imprison Quark&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:08.647 --> 00:23:10.954
&lt;i&gt;in exchange for 76%&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:10.997 --> 00:23:12.999
&lt;i&gt;of all his franchises' profits.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:13.043 --> 00:23:15.175
- Yes, yes, it's on him.

00:23:15.219 --> 00:23:18.352
Th-Th-That table wants more
top-shelf Tamarian mead,

00:23:18.396 --> 00:23:20.485
a-and they're insisting
that it's on the house.

00:23:20.529 --> 00:23:22.182
Just bring them what they want.

00:23:22.226 --> 00:23:25.447
I thought
you said your plan

00:23:25.490 --> 00:23:27.318
would make us both happy.

00:23:27.361 --> 00:23:29.625
Well, you're happier being poor
than in prison, aren't you?

00:23:29.668 --> 00:23:31.061
No!

00:23:31.104 --> 00:23:32.628
Sorry, I didn't
win over your friends.

00:23:32.671 --> 00:23:35.500
Please, even better,
now they're scared of you.

00:23:35.544 --> 00:23:36.849
- Shh, shh.

00:23:36.893 --> 00:23:38.024
She's looking, she's looking,

00:23:38.068 --> 00:23:39.504
- don't look.

00:23:39.548 --> 00:23:42.681
One Risa Colada
and a Mind Meld. Mariner.

00:23:42.725 --> 00:23:45.249
You'd better have a stack
of latinum down there.

00:23:45.292 --> 00:23:48.295
Uh, nope. But I do have a copy
of that hologram

00:23:48.339 --> 00:23:49.645
with your head on Kira's body.

00:23:49.688 --> 00:23:51.516
Impossible.
I erased that.

00:23:51.560 --> 00:23:52.909
- How about we clear my tab?

00:23:52.952 --> 00:23:54.998
Unless you're not afraid
of Kira seeing this.

00:23:55.041 --> 00:23:56.390
- Mariner.

00:23:56.434 --> 00:23:57.653
I was wondering
when you'd show up.

00:23:57.696 --> 00:23:59.306
Are you guys
telling war stories?

00:23:59.350 --> 00:24:01.700
I was just clearing her tab,
for old time's sake.

00:24:01.744 --> 00:24:03.136
What is on that chip?

00:24:03.180 --> 00:24:04.181
- No!
- No, give that to me,

00:24:04.224 --> 00:24:05.225
give it to me.

00:24:05.269 --> 00:24:07.445
- Quark.

00:24:09.926 --> 00:24:12.363
- Dabo!
- Listen, you could

00:24:12.406 --> 00:24:14.017
walk out of here
with all that latinum,

00:24:14.060 --> 00:24:16.628
that germy, dirty latinum, or...

00:24:16.672 --> 00:24:20.545
a gift certificate for twice its
value at our Quark's gift store.

00:24:20.589 --> 00:24:22.634
Quark's bucks.
I'll take it.

00:24:22.678 --> 00:24:24.897
We don't even use
money in Starfleet anyway.

00:24:24.941 --> 00:24:27.160
What?

00:24:27.204 --> 00:24:29.511
Oh, it was good to see you
today, old-timer.

00:24:29.554 --> 00:24:32.426
Yes. The prophets smiled
on both of us.

00:24:32.470 --> 00:24:35.081
Thanks for having my back
when the klisht hit the fan.

00:24:35.125 --> 00:24:37.519
- Just doing my job.
- Now I do owe you one.

00:24:37.562 --> 00:24:38.868
Wait, what? No.

00:24:38.911 --> 00:24:41.392
- No, no, no. Hey, come on.

00:24:41.435 --> 00:24:43.220
Gotcha.

00:24:43.263 --> 00:24:46.353
But then the way you, like,
dance-flip-konked that guard,

00:24:46.397 --> 00:24:47.790
I was like, damn!

00:24:47.833 --> 00:24:49.139
I didn't know
Tendi could do that.

00:24:49.182 --> 00:24:50.227
Well,
so you're not embarrassed

00:24:50.270 --> 00:24:51.445
to be friends with someone

00:24:51.489 --> 00:24:53.447
whose family was into pirating?

00:24:53.491 --> 00:24:55.754
No way.
It's a part of who you are.

00:24:55.798 --> 00:24:57.060
I like hearing about it.

00:24:57.103 --> 00:24:58.931
Thanks, Rutherford. From now on,

00:24:58.975 --> 00:25:01.673
I'm going to embrace my past
and what comes with it.

00:25:01.717 --> 00:25:04.241
Uh, what are you gonna do
with the tooth?

00:25:04.284 --> 00:25:06.548
I don't know, i-it's actually
kind of gross, isn't it?

00:25:06.591 --> 00:25:08.071
I'll take that.

00:25:08.114 --> 00:25:09.725
Rule of Acquisition number nine.

00:25:09.768 --> 00:25:13.380
&lt;i&gt;Opportunity plus instinct
equals profit.&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:14.180 --> 00:26:18.180
Chirp.
